Author: rpone <rponeawa@qq.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 17:09:29 2026 +0800

    feat(cheeseburger): keep the frame buffer log and drop the Linux image
    
    SerialDxe is only built for non-release targets, but UniXNU writes its log
    through EFI_SERIAL_IO_PROTOCOL and this board has no UART in the UEFI image.
    Include it in release so the log and the DEBUG output reach the frame buffer
    console that FrameBufferSerialPortLib already drives at 0x9d400000.
    
    LinuxSimpleMassStorage embeds a 6.9 MiB Linux image that the B line never
    boots.  Dropping it shrinks the compressed firmware volume from 2.60 MiB to
    1.00 MiB, so the 6.0 MiB FD now has 4.97 MiB free for the boot stack.

